message:
I am thinking...: This is very important. Looking at lines 740-750:

```c
if(1 == ps_codec->i4_pic_present && 0 == ps_codec->s_parse.i4_end_of_frame)
{
    slice_header_t *ps_slice_hdr_next;
    ps_codec->i4_slice_error = 1;
    ...
    ps_slice_hdr_next->i2_ctb_x = -1;
    ps_slice_hdr_next->i2_ctb_y = -1;

    ihevcd_parse_slice_data(ps_codec);
    ASSERT(ps_codec->s_parse.i4_end_of_frame != 0);
}
```

So when a picture is present but the frame isn't fully parsed (incomplete data), the decoder sets `i4_slice_error = 1` and calls `ihevcd_parse_slice_data` which will continue parsing/processing. This is the error concealment path!

Under error conditions, the decoder will still try to complete the frame, and it will call the processing pipeline including SAO. This is key - even with malformed CABAC data, the decoder will still try to process all CTBs and run SAO.

Now, when slice_error is set, `ihevcd_parse_slice_data` handles it by essentially filling in dummy CTB data and advancing the CTB counter. This should trigger the SAO processing pipeline.

Let me look at how `ihevcd_parse_slice_data` handles errors:

